<p>I kind of figured he would write them at night. He has to sleep at some point, and documenting this kind of stuff in a diary seems like a thing a pilot in the 40s would do.</p>
<p>Anyway this was pretty good. There were a lot of places where the language was a little informal. The only thing I find weird is that you say &quot;it has caused no direct fatalities through its actions&quot;, which might technically be true but the only 2 accounts we have of people encountering this thing, they both mysteriously disappear.<br />
Still, I like the concept and the diary was decent enough for an upvote.</p>

